  "enhanced_information": "In DiGeorge syndrome, which is associated with 22q11.2 deletion, aplastic thymus is a common finding leading to lymphopenia and absent follicles in the lymph nodes. Hypertrophy of Hassall's corpuscles is not typically seen in this condition. Hypercellular bone marrow is not a characteristic feature. An accessory spleen may be present in some cases of DiGeorge syndrome."
